        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a level-persistence prior of 13.4 from the seven-year corrected-methodology sample. Judgmental adjustments in percentage points are momentum 0.0, one-off 0.0, incremental SNAP policy effects +0.6, and macro improvement -0.1, giving 13.4 + 0.6 - 0.1 = 13.9. These adjustment magnitudes are forecasting assumptions, not official estimates; the increased child credit is already represented in the anchor. Successive historical changes are [-2.8, -4.5, 6.9, 1.5, 0.0, -0.1], with mean 0.166667 and squared deviations summing to 77.793333. Sample sigma = 3.944448 percentage points = sqrt(77.793333/5); 1.28*sigma = 5.048893. Narrow that half-width by a judgmental factor of 0.60 because emergency pandemic transfers and their reversal dominate dispersion and are not the central regime. The corrected methodology is already observed, so no speculative transition shift is added. The resulting predictive sigma of 2.366669 remains above the ordinary 2023\u20132025 transition sigma of 0.896289 multiplied by sqrt(2), retaining room for the two-year horizon, policy implementation, and first-print measurement risk. The nominal 80% normal interval has half-width 1.28*2.366669 = 3.029336, giving 10.870664 to 16.929336, reported as [10.87, 16.93]."
